<title>JAPAN: Total of 260,000 shares cut from JR West offer.</title>
<headline>Total of 260,000 shares cut from JR West offer.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese National Railways (JNR) Settlement Corp said on Friday that 260,000 Japan Railway Co Ltd (JR West) shares have been withdrawn from a public offering.</p>
<p>The shares account for 27.3 percent of the total issue originally planned for the offering, it said.</p>
<p>The number of shares unsold ahead of the listing on October 8, including those left unsold at the auction in August, totalled 334,344. The remainder would be sold later, the settlement corp said.</p>
